 "_about": "Round 40 (Robert: 'growing your own swarm, it would be nice to utilize them as a utility ... build its own skill tree, be able to design different nanites for different functions, cost qi and resources to research and connect while meditating ... a research tree for splitting the mind or diverting the nanites' function on more than one thing at a time. Wetware, hardware, cybernetics and power armor come into play in late game. The game should feel more techy as we get further on but qi and equipment still matter. Build it modular.'). ONE ENGINE (scripts/systems/Research.gd) reads this file: add a node here and it's in the game. Kinds: design (connected into the swarm's BANDWIDTH, runs on qi upkeep, can be TUNED with a material), passive (always on once researched), unlock (opens a feature: split meditation, background work), install (wetware / hardware / cybernetics / power armour: costs BODY LOAD, which grows with your realm and how clean your meridians are). Research takes sitting time (Research as your meditation focus), qi (a share of a step, paid at the start) and materials. Connecting, tuning and installing are done while you sit.",
